              "content": "Maestro reads the workspace's ledgers (asks, work, loops, ticks, initiatives, fleet), types them in Rust, and serves the same answers to the CLI, to any MCP harness and to an MCP App you can touch. Owner actions arrive only with a verified principal; orchestration arrives last, on top of the fleet skill and bstack, which stay as they are.",
